;; EXPECT: sort-error
;; Book chapter 4: a clamp is not a free-standing property.
;;
;; This program is REJECTED, and the book shows it because the rejection is the
;; lesson. `:idempotent` and `:nilpotent` are clamps on a multiset of children, so
;; they presuppose that the children ARE a multiset, which is what `:assoc` and
;; `:comm` together establish. Declaring a clamp on an operator whose children are
;; an ordered, fixed-arity list asks the engine to bound a count that does not
;; exist.
;;
;; The engine reports, and exits 1:
;;   sort error: :idempotent/:nilpotent require :assoc :comm
;;
;; The test suite asserts that this file keeps failing this way, which is why the
;; error text above can be trusted to be current.

(sort E)
(function a () E)

;; No structural attribute, so `dup` is an ordinary binary Plain node.
(function dup (E E) E :idempotent)

(check (= (dup a a) a))
